{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Living soul.</b> That there be in it vitality." "<b>Swarming thing.</b> Every living creature that is not high off the ground is called שֶׁרֶץ: among birds — such as flies; among creeping things — such as ants, beetles, and worms; among creatures — such as the weasel, mouse, and skink, and the like; and all fish."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:07.501081157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}